B.VV=new A.tG("ROP","Test and consolidate your clinical understanding of ROP prevention, screening protocols, timing criteria, analgesia, zone/stage treatment, and post-discharge surveillance.","Multiple choice questions covering KPIs, prevention measures, screening arrangements, pre-exam fasting/preparation, gestational age eligibility, screening timing, zone treatment, and Stage 1 management.","Real-life bedside vignettes including oxygen titration, timely screening KPI calculations, transfer documentation, anti-VEGF surveillance, and aggressive ROP follow-up.","Retinopathy of Prematurity (ROP)","8 MCQs and 8 bedside clinical case scenarios based on ICMR / DHR STW guidelines.",B.zM,B.zY)
B.aaR=s(["22+0 to 31+6 weeks","24+0 to 33+6 weeks","26+0 to 35+6 weeks","28+0 to 36+6 weeks"],t.s)
B.Z2=new A.cy("ancs_mcq_1","According to the STW, antenatal corticosteroids are given to pregnant women at which gestational age (with a high likelihood of preterm birth within the next 7 days)?",B.aaR,1,'WHEN TO GIVE: "Pregnant women at 24+0 to 33+6 weeks of gestation with a high likelihood of preterm birth within the next 7 days".',"When to give",null,'ICMR/DHR STW "Antenatal Corticosteroids for Preterm Birth" (August 2026), WHEN TO GIVE')
B.abL=s(["Dexamethasone sodium phosphate 6 mg IM every 12 hours x 4 doses","Dexamethasone sodium phosphate 12 mg IM every 24 hours x 4 doses","Dexamethasone sodium phosphate 6 mg IV every 6 hours x 2 doses","Dexamethasone sodium phosphate 6 mg orally once daily x 4 days"],t.s)
B.Zy=new A.cy("ancs_mcq_2","Which regimen does the STW give under DRUG & DOSE?",B.abL,0,'DRUG & DOSE: "DEXAMETHASONE SODIUM PHOSPHATE 6mg IM EVERY 12 HOURS X 4 DOSES".',"Drug & dose",null,u.aS)
B.aaq=s(["It is given as a single dose","It is effective, low-cost, widely available and more heat-stable","It is the only corticosteroid available in India","It does not need to be given intramuscularly"],t.s)
B.ZE=new A.cy("ancs_mcq_3","Why does the STW prefer dexamethasone?",B.aaq,1,'DRUG & DOSE: "Dexamethasone is preferred: it is effective, low-cost, widely available and more heat-stable". The STW adds that the betamethasone regimen requires an acetate + phosphate preparation, which is not available in India.',"Drug & dose",null,u.aS)
B.a7d=s(["PPROM without clinical infection","Antepartum Hemorrhage","Severe pre-eclampsia/eclampsia","Multiple pregnancy alone"],t.s)
B.Zd=new A.cy("ancs_mcq_4","All of the following are listed in the STW as causes of a high likelihood of preterm birth within the next 7 days EXCEPT:",B.a7d,3,"ELIGIBILITY CRITERIA 1 lists: spontaneous preterm labour, PPROM without clinical infection, Antepartum Hemorrhage, Severe pre-eclampsia/eclampsia, and planned preterm birth for maternal/fetal indication. Multiple pregnancy is not one of them; it appears under SPECIAL SITUATIONS as a reason NOT to withhold ACS when otherwise eligible.","Eligibility criteria",null,'ICMR/DHR STW "Antenatal Corticosteroids for Preterm Birth" (August 2026), ELIGIBILITY CRITERIA')
B.a54=s([u.m,"Fetal growth restriction","Hypertensive disorders","Diabetes in pregnancy"],t.s)
B.Zf=new A.cy("ancs_mcq_5","Which of these is a reason NOT to give ACS according to the STW?",B.a54,0,'WHEN NOT TO GIVE: "Clinical chorioamnionitis or systemic maternal infection". SPECIAL SITUATIONS: "When otherwise eligible, do not withhold ACS because of: multiple pregnancy, fetal growth restriction, hypertensive disorders, or diabetes in pregnancy".',"When not to give",null,'ICMR/DHR STW "Antenatal Corticosteroids for Preterm Birth" (August 2026), WHEN NOT TO GIVE; SPECIAL SITUATIONS')
B.a5_=s(["Repeat courses are given every week until 34 weeks","Two repeat courses may be given if needed","ONE repeat course only, if GA 24+0 to 33+6 weeks, high likelihood of preterm birth within the next 7 days, and the previous course was started \u22657 days earlier","A repeat course is never given"],t.s)
B.Z7=new A.cy("ancs_mcq_6","What does the STW say about a repeat course of ACS?",B.a5_,2,'WHEN TO GIVE REPEAT COURSE: "Give ONE repeat course only if ALL criteria are met": GA 24+0 to 33+6 weeks; high likelihood of preterm birth within the next 7 days; the previous ACS course was started \u22657 days earlier. "Do NOT give more than one repeat course (More than one repeat course may cause fetal harm, and is not recommended)".',"Repeat course",null,u.eo)
B.a3o=s(["Complete all 4 doses before referral","Give the first dose of ACS before referral, without delaying referral/transfer to complete the course","Give no ACS and refer immediately","Keep the woman until birth and refer the newborn"],t.s)
B.ZC=new A.cy("ancs_mcq_7","What may a level I facility do for an eligible pregnant woman who needs referral?",B.a3o,1,'REFERRAL/TRANSFER: "Level I facilities can give the first dose of ACS before referral, provided the pregnant woman meets the eligibility criteria, but referral/transfer should not be delayed to complete the course".',"Referral/transfer",null,u.X)
B.acb=s(["\u226550%","\u226570%","\u226580%","\u226595%"],t.s)
B.Zi=new A.cy("ancs_mcq_8","What is the STW target for ACS coverage?",B.acb,2,"KEY PERFORMANCE INDICATORS: ACS coverage = women at 24+0\u201333+6 weeks identified with high likelihood of preterm birth who received \u22651 ACS dose \xd7 100 / all such women (Target: \u226580%). The target for appropriate ACS use is \u226595%.","KPIs",null,'ICMR/DHR STW "Antenatal Corticosteroids for Preterm Birth" (August 2026), KEY PERFORMANCE INDICATORS (KPIs)')
B.aaL=s([B.Z2,B.Zy,B.ZE,B.Zd,B.Zf,B.Z7,B.ZC,B.Zi],t.tw)
B.a5Q=s(["Wait for labour to start before giving ACS","Give ACS: dexamethasone sodium phosphate 6 mg IM every 12 hours x 4 doses, starting promptly","Do not give ACS because of PPROM","Give ACS only if birth will be delayed until the full course is completed"],t.s)
B.Zs=new A.cy("ancs_case_1","What should be done as per the STW?",B.a5Q,1,'All five ELIGIBILITY CRITERIA are met (24+0 to 33+6 weeks; PPROM without clinical infection; GA assessed accurately; no chorioamnionitis or systemic infection; adequate childbirth and preterm newborn care). "IMPORTANT: Start ACS promptly once eligibility criteria are met, even if the full course may not be completed before birth".',"Eligibility","A pregnant woman at 30+2 weeks (GA confirmed by early USG) has PPROM without clinical infection. There is no clinical chorioamnionitis or systemic infection. Your facility has adequate childbirth care and preterm newborn care including CPAP. She has not received ACS before.",'ICMR/DHR STW "Antenatal Corticosteroids for Preterm Birth" (August 2026), ELIGIBILITY CRITERIA; DRUG & DOSE')
B.a3p=s(["Give ACS routinely","Do NOT routinely use ACS at \u226534+0 weeks","Give a half dose","Give one dose and refer"],t.s)
B.Zc=new A.cy("ancs_case_2","What does the STW advise about ACS?",B.a3p,1,'WHEN NOT TO GIVE: "Routine use at \u226534 weeks". DON\'Ts: "Do NOT routinely use ACS at \u226534+0 weeks or give more than one repeat course".',"When not to give","A pregnant woman at 35+1 weeks is in spontaneous preterm labour with regular contractions and cervical change.",'ICMR/DHR STW "Antenatal Corticosteroids for Preterm Birth" (August 2026), WHEN NOT TO GIVE; DONTs')
B.aam=s(["Give ACS promptly","Give ACS after the first dose of antibiotics",u.eV,"Give a repeat course instead"],t.s)
B.Z0=new A.cy("ancs_case_3","What does the STW advise about ACS?",B.aam,2,'Criterion 3 ("No clinical chorioamnionitis or systemic maternal infection") is not met. WHEN NOT TO GIVE: "Clinical chorioamnionitis or systemic maternal infection". DON\'Ts: "Do NOT give ACS in clinical chorioamnionitis or systemic maternal infection".',"When not to give","A pregnant woman at 28+4 weeks with spontaneous preterm labour has been diagnosed with clinical chorioamnionitis.",'ICMR/DHR STW "Antenatal Corticosteroids for Preterm Birth" (August 2026), ELIGIBILITY CRITERIA; WHEN NOT TO GIVE')
B.adg=s(["Give ONE repeat course","No further ACS can ever be given","Give two repeat courses 7 days apart","Wait until 34 weeks"],t.s)
B.Z8=new A.cy("ancs_case_4","What should be done as per the STW?",B.adg,0,'WHEN TO GIVE REPEAT COURSE: ONE repeat course if ALL are met: GA 24+0 to 33+6 weeks; high likelihood of preterm birth within the next 7 days; the previous ACS course was started \u22657 days earlier. "Do NOT give more than one repeat course".',"Repeat course","A pregnant woman at 31+0 weeks received one ACS course that was started 10 days ago. She now has antepartum hemorrhage with a high likelihood of preterm birth within the next 7 days. She meets the other eligibility criteria and has not had a repeat course.",u.eo)
B.a7f=s(["Complete the full ACS course before referral","Give the first dose of ACS and refer for in-utero transfer to a facility with at least level II care (CPAP), without delaying referral to complete the course","Refer without giving ACS","Keep her at the level I facility until birth"],t.s)
B.Ze=new A.cy("ancs_case_5","What does the STW advise?",B.a7f,1,'REFERRAL/TRANSFER: "Pregnant women with likelihood of early preterm birth should be referred to a facility (in-utero transfer) with at least level II care (CPAP) for preterm infants"; "Level I facilities can give the first dose of ACS before referral, provided the pregnant woman meets the eligibility criteria, but referral/transfer should not be delayed to complete the course".',"Referral/transfer","At a level I facility without CPAP, a pregnant woman at 29+3 weeks with severe pre-eclampsia meets the ACS eligibility criteria (preterm newborn care including CPAP is ensured at the receiving facility).",u.X)
